Following up on my January comment. #32081 helped (~68s to ~60s in @junuxyz's test above) but it still pays the strided gather on the CPU, just over smaller slices. I took the direction @robertgshaw2-redhat suggested to its conclusion in #47580: keep the copy source as the contiguous on-disk slab and do the transpose as a strided write into the parameter on the GPU side. No copy of the loaded weight is kept in GPU memory at any point.

On 1x A100-80G (warm cache): per-copy time on Scout-size fp8 expert slabs goes 62.8ms to 4.0ms (15.8x), and end to end on a 24-layer Scout FP8 truncation (full model doesn't fit one 80G card) load time goes 18.8s to 12.5s. This applies to any fused-MoE checkpoint that arrives transposed, not just Llama-4/ModelOpt. If anyone can run the full model on cc >= 8.9 hardware I'd appreciate the datapoint.

@pratheeknathani #46766 takes the same approach as #32081, so the ~60s numbers above should carry over to it.

